finding: Normal-map tangent generation does not use the transformed texture coordinate. src/extras/gltf/gltf.ts:generateSceneTangents selects the extension's texCoord but passes the untransformed UV array to generateTangents and generateMorphTangents. standard-material.ts samples normalUv after T*R*S but interprets it through ctx.tangent unchanged. For meshes without supplied TANGENT this violates glTF's MikkTSpace generation from the coordinates associated with the normal texture, and rotating/mirroring a normal texture gives the wrong tangent frame despite the coordinate probes passing. Independently reproduced without editing: load fixtures/normal-uv1.gltf JSON, set normalTexture.extensions.KHR_texture_transform.rotation=PI/2, parse and generateSceneTangents: tangents are [0,1,0,1] per vertex. Applying the README's rotation matrix to UV1 first and independently calling generateTangents produces [-1,0,0,1]. The GPU probe supplies a fixed tangent and constant UVs and its normal expectation expressly uses the unchanged frame, so it cannot catch this. Correct generated base and morph tangent frames and add a transformed-coordinate normal-frame regression.
